+# Legacy companion custody
+
+Deploy this module together with the QuestSync custody changes. The shared characters-DB migration and offline rollout procedure live in the paired QuestSync tree: `sql/companion-custody.sql` and `docs/companion-custody.md`. An empty custody table intentionally leaves the old records unverified and reserved; no startup sweep rolls old bodies back to pool names or clears their login flags.
+
+`.companion create` only claims reviewed stock assigned to `legacy`. Existing companions need independently verified custody before summon, dismiss, or companion-memory participation. `.companion forget` and `.companion destroy yes` require a safely dismissed body and request offline retirement; neither wipes, renames, or recycles the body. The owner slot stays reserved until staff finalizes the retirement. Do not run an older allocator alongside these guards.
+
+Death Knights are unavailable for new claims and are excluded from stock regardless of level; do not enroll them as `free`. This does not affect independently verified owned Death Knights.
+
+Run `python -B -m unittest discover -s tests` for the legacy contract checks. QuestSync also has an opt-in isolated MySQL suite exercising SQL from both modules.
